research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8752-{"id":"cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The separated uniformization theorem is standard, but the item exposes DC and the library Tychonoff convention. Empty carrier is currently a counterexample, and T1/Hausdorff bridge citations are incomplete.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8753-{"id":"def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU gives exactly these entourage formulas under an explicit Hausdorff hypothesis, while the item correctly defines them for arbitrary, possibly non-Hausdorff topological groups. Dropping Hausdorff is standard established mathematics, but it is a genuine hypothesis delta and no matching source surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8754-{"id":"thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU states the natural group uniformities induce the group topology in its Hausdorff uniformity section. The same proof works for arbitrary topological groups and inversion interchanges the two, but no located source states this exact non-Hausdorff package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8755-{"id":"def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU and Rosendal define the upper join and Roelcke meet with the displayed basic entourages for Hausdorff or Polish groups. The formulas extend unchanged to arbitrary topological groups, a standard convention, but the published domain is broader than the located sources.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8756-{"id":"cor-topological-groups-are-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Uniformizability of every topological group and complete regularity of uniformizable spaces are standard, but the item states their precise DC-dependent composition under the non-Hausdorff convention. No source states that exact package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log:8757:{"id":"ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The homeomorphism h(x)=x/(1+|x|) is a standard bounded-coordinate example; searches found only informal exact discussions, not an allowed source for this witness. The verification shows established mathematics, not novelty. Its triangle-inequality citation is wrong.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8758-{"id":"fs-a-compatible-uniformity-is-unique","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Nonuniqueness of compatible uniformities on noncompact spaces is standard; Wodzicki proves uniqueness only compactly and gives continuous-not-uniformly-continuous witnesses. No source states this exact false universal plus pullback refutation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8759-{"id":"ex-additive-group-uniformity-on-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sourced group formulas and commutativity make all four group uniformities equal the usual metric uniformity on additive R. No source states this exact four-way example, but it is standard, not novel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8760-{"id":"ex-pointwise-but-not-uniform-convergence-on-a-countable-domain","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Moving-tail indicator functions are a canonical pointwise-not-uniform witness, but no reputable source with this exact N-to-{0,1} construction surfaced. The verification is direct and established; its discrete-uniformity citation is incomplete.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-8761-{"id":"cex-k-topology-is-not-uniformizable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-31.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. ETSU notes prove the K-topology Hausdorff but not regular, while uniformizable spaces are regular. Their composition gives this conclusion, but no source states it as one proposition; it is standard, not novel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
