research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-alpha-d2-recovery.log-13871-+{"id":"def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU and Rosendal define the upper join and Roelcke meet with the displayed basic entourages for Hausdorff or Polish groups. The formulas extend unchanged to arbitrary topological groups, a standard convention, but the published domain is broader than the located sources. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The upper join and Roelcke meet, with intersection and left-right composite bases, are standard topological-group uniformities. The formulas require no separation axiom, so extending their usual sourced domain to arbitrary topological groups is established mathematics.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
