research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-169876-+{"id":"ex-additive-group-uniformity-on-r","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The sourced group formulas and commutativity make all four group uniformities equal the usual metric uniformity on additive R. No source states this exact four-way example, but it is standard, not novel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-169877-+{"id":"ex-pointwise-but-not-uniform-convergence-on-a-countable-domain","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":[],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Moving-tail indicator functions are a canonical pointwise-not-uniform witness, but no reputable source with this exact N-to-{0,1} construction surfaced. The verification is direct and established; its discrete-uniformity citation is incomplete.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-169878-+{"id":"ex-closed-unit-interval-has-one-compatible-uniformity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf"],"rationale":"Vienna Theorem 9.4.14 gives the unique compatible uniformity on every compact Hausdorff space, and the metric construction identifies it on [0,1]. The item is this standard specialization.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-169879-+{"id":"cex-k-topology-is-not-uniformizable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://faculty.etsu.edu/gardnerr/5357/notes/Munkres-31.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. ETSU notes prove the K-topology Hausdorff but not regular, while uniformizable spaces are regular. Their composition gives this conclusion, but no source states it as one proposition; it is standard, not novel.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
