research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:234834:[L1] The map $h(x)=x/(1+|x|)$ is a homeomorphism $\mathbb R\to(-1,1)$ but not a uniform isomorphism for the usual metric uniformities ([[ex-r-and-open-interval-homeomorphic-not-uniformly-isomorphic]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-234835-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-234836-[L2] Uniformizable means induced by a uniformity, and a uniform isomorphism has uniformly continuous inverse ([[def-uniformizable-space]], [[def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism]]).
